    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2UThF91LQrHDWWAJF3dXMZi)_\n\nColumn width and word wrap of the exc table are now part of the spec, so a saved view keeps them with its columns.\n\n- New spec keys `:column-widths` (alist `(COLUMN . WIDTH)`, `t` for the columns not listed) and `:wrap` (`wrap` or `fit`). Views, the dynamic block and the menu carry them like any other key; vui and Org ignore them.\n- `wrap` keeps the widths and wraps long text onto more lines. `fit` sizes each column to its longest text, up to `sp-collec-query-exc-max-width` (80). An explicit width always wins.\n- New options `sp-collec-query-exc-wrap` and `sp-collec-query-exc-max-width`; `sp-collec-query-exc-column-widths` stays the default. A width in the spec overrides them.\n- Menu: `w` sets the width of one column (or `other`), `W` cycles the wrap between default, `wrap` and `fit`.\n- Docs and CHANGELOG updated.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container, and exc is not installed). Branch name could not be renamed to `169-…`: the proxy blocks branch renames.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBvN7MM96hTgFDoZmk)_",
